Subject: SAIL Ontology Interoperability Profile

& [SpecificationIdentity] is the canonical SJS research specification
  + [specification_uuid] is 1332ebdb-4673-43c1-806a-d15063dbf092
  + [status] is research_profile_not_implementation_authority
  + [purpose] is distinguish reusable ontology standards from SAIL-native operational semantics

& [StandardsDelineation] is the semantic layer boundary
  + [RDF] is graph identity and subject-predicate-object assertion representation
  + [RDFS] is lightweight vocabulary, hierarchy, domain, range, and entailment
  + [OWL] is expressive ontology axioms, inference, equivalence, disjointness, restrictions, and consistency reasoning under open-world semantics
  + [SHACL] is operational validation of concrete RDF graphs against node and property shapes
  + [SKOS] is concept schemes, preferred and alternate labels, semantic relations, and mappings
  + [PROV_O] is provenance of entities, activities, agents, generation, use, and derivation
  + [SchemaOrg] is a broad pragmatic external vocabulary for common entities, relations, and actions
  = correction: RDFS infers and OWL constrains is incomplete because OWL also infers while SHACL is the more direct validation and constraint layer

& [WorldAssumptionBoundary] is the distinction required by SOP
  + [open_world] is missing knowledge does not imply falsity
  + [closed_operational_validation] is a required field missing from a program is a fault
  = must: not use OWL alone as form-completeness or database-record validation
  = must: use explicit validation for must, never, cardinality, datatype, path, and closed-shape requirements

& [SAILReuseMap] is the candidate compatibility mapping
  + [SemanticAnchor] maps provisionally to skos:Concept
  + [ContextualAnchorSet] maps provisionally to skos:ConceptScheme or a named graph
  + [preferred_term] maps to skos:prefLabel
  + [alias_term] maps to skos:altLabel or skos:hiddenLabel
  + [broader_narrower_relation] maps to SKOS hierarchy relations
  + [typed_hierarchy] maps to rdfs:subClassOf or rdfs:subPropertyOf where their semantics fit
  + [program_structure_constraint] maps to SHACL node and property shapes
  + [semantic_impossibility] may map to OWL disjointness or restrictions
  + [turn_job_file_inference_lineage] maps to PROV-O Entity, Activity, Agent, generation, use, and derivation
  + [public_entity_interchange] may map to schema.org
  = must: preserve context and provenance rather than collapse competing meanings through indiscriminate owl:sameAs

& [SAILNativeBoundary] is what recognized ontologies do not presently supply
  + [attention_state_transition] is explicit focus, hold, release, admit, exclude, pull, push, peek, and return behavior
  + [purpose_bound_inference] is inference governed by declared purpose and faculty boundaries
  + [faculty_program] is Honesty, Security, Refiner, Scribe, Weaver, Planner, and Observer coordination
  + [effect_authority] is separation of semantic read authority from mutation and execution authority
  + [reentry] is restoration of purpose, attention state, unresolved frontier, and provenance
  + [executable_SOP] is typed attention and inference programs with observable effects and faults
  = conclusion: recognized ontology standards provide substrate and interoperability profiles, not the complete SAIL operating semantics

& [CandidateArchitecture] is the smallest standards-aligned stack
  + [layer_1] is stable SAIL identities with an RDF-compatible graph projection
  + [layer_2] is SKOS-compatible semantic anchors and concept schemes
  + [layer_3] is RDFS lightweight hierarchy and entailment
  + [layer_4] is a bounded OWL profile such as OWL 2 RL only where justified by tests
  + [layer_5] is SHACL validation for structures, programs, and effects
  + [layer_6] is PROV-O-compatible lineage
  + [layer_7] is optional schema.org mapping for external interchange
  = must: not commit the physical database backend merely because the interchange model is RDF-compatible

& [ResearchProofSlice] is the next bounded experiment
  + [corpus] is ten to twenty representative SAIL primitive, anchor, program, and provenance records
  + [proof_1] is query terms and recover matching structures and authoritative files
  + [proof_2] is infer a type or relation hierarchy
  + [proof_3] is reject a malformed SAIL program with an inspectable validation report
  + [proof_4] is trace a result through job, model, turn, source, and file
  + [proof_5] is preserve contextual uncertainty and incompatible perspectives without global identity collapse
  = decision_gate: adopt only standards whose mappings preserve SAIL meaning and improve inspection, validation, or exchange

& [RequirementSet] is the traceable research requirement collection
  + [ONT-001] is separate graph representation, entailment, ontology reasoning, and validation
  + [ONT-002] is evaluate SKOS as the semantic-anchor vocabulary substrate
  + [ONT-003] is evaluate SHACL as the SAIL program and record validation substrate
  + [ONT-004] is evaluate PROV-O as the turn, job, file, and inference lineage substrate
  + [ONT-005] is treat schema.org as optional external vocabulary rather than SAIL core authority
  + [ONT-006] is preserve SAIL-native attention, purpose, faculty, effect, and reentry semantics
  + [ONT-007] is validate the profile through a bounded representative corpus before backend selection

& [SJSProcessingTrace] is the ontology interoperability trace
  + [fold_1_subject] is recognized ontology reuse for SAIL declarations, inference, constraints, anchors, and provenance
  + [fold_2_boundary] is standards-compatible substrate and exchange outside; SAIL operational semantics inside
  + [fold_3_data_design] is stable identities, concepts, schemes, typed relations, shapes, named contexts, and provenance
  + [fold_4_governance] is mappings remain provisional until semantic preservation and inspection proofs pass
  + [fold_5_solution_shape] is a small interoperability corpus and four-axis query, inference, validation, and provenance proof
  + [fold_6_fault_review] is open-world validation confusion, owl:sameAs collapse, schema.org overreach, backend lock-in, and unbounded ontology complexity
  + [fold_7_phase_lock] is research profile stable; implementation authority absent pending proof

